window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["39"]={"https://theconversation.com/how-political-disagreement-with-our-neighbours-relates-to-whether-we-bother-casting-a-ballot-295642":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"e6a9e7bf8334e9a85daa16d5ca823cb4ac22d6299f779475f170cbfe38368619","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-political-disagreement-with-our-neighbours-relates-to-whether-we-bother-casting-a-ballot-295642","bytes":183813,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How political disagreement with our neighbours relates to whether we bother casting a ballot","by":[{"n":"Md Mujahedul Islam","r":"SSHRC Postdoctoral Fellow, Department of Government, Cornell University"}],"pub":"2026-11-02T17:28:40Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In the 2025 federal election, Canadians voted at ",["the highest rate since 1993","https://www.elections.ca/res/rec/eval/pes2025/evt/evt_e.pdf"],". Explanations for high or low turnout usually focus on the national election campaign, including how close the race was and what seemed to be at stake."]},{"k":"p","s":["As lead author of a ",["new study published in the Canadian Journal of Political Science","https://doi.org/10.1017/S0008423926101462"],", I worked with my co-authors — Daniel Rubenson, Roosmarijn de Geus, Benjamin Allen Stevens and Peter John Loewen — to look close to home and examine how someone’s political views compare with those of the people around them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our research shows that people whose views closely match the average views in their riding are less likely to vote than those whose views differ moderately. Similarly, people whose views differ extensively from those around them are less likely to vote. In short, voting peaks at moderate levels of disagreement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Measuring disagreement next door"]},{"k":"p","s":["We used the ",["Local Parliament Project","https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/DACHKP"],", an online survey of more than 31,000 Canadians conducted during the 2015 federal election campaign, in our research. It included respondents from nearly every riding, which allowed us to compare each person’s views with those of others in the same riding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Research shows labels like “left” and “right” ",["mean different things to different people","https://doi.org/10.1007/s11109-016-9368-2"],". We, therefore, measured political views using people’s positions on 37 specific issues, such as taxes, health care and immigration."]},{"k":"p","s":["This allowed us to see how far each person’s views were from their neighbours’ in the same riding, and the diversity of opinions across the riding as a whole. This captured different information. For example, a riding’s voters can be largely like-minded, yet some people living there can still hold differing views about specific issues."]},{"k":"h","s":["A sweet spot for voting"]},{"k":"p","s":["We found that a person whose views are very similar to their riding’s average has a predicted 83 per cent chance of voting. A person at the opposite extreme has a predicted 63 per cent chance, though this estimate is less precise. People halfway between these extremes have the highest likelihood of voting, at 90 per cent."]},{"k":"p","s":["These patterns hold after we account for factors that include age, education, income, how close the local race was and how much parties campaigned. Ridings with tight races in 2015 did not have higher turnout than those where one party won easily."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our riding-level analysis shows a similar picture. Predicted turnout is 65.7 per cent at the lowest level of opinion diversity, rises to 68.7 per cent at the mid-point and falls to 65.3 per cent at the highest. However, these differences are not statistically significant once we account for other factors."]},{"k":"p","s":["The link between a person’s views and voting also varies with the local mix of views. In ridings with a wide range of views, voting peaks at smaller differences and drops off more steeply for people whose views differ extensively."]},{"k":"p","s":["So two people equally far from how most of their neighbours intend to vote can have different chances of showing up to cast a ballot depending on their riding."]},{"k":"h","s":["Disagreement can boost voter turnout"]},{"k":"p","s":["When our views match those around us, we rarely hear disagreement. Politics can feel settled, and our vote may seem unnecessary. Some disagreement changes that. It makes political differences more visible and the choice on the ballot feel more important."]},{"k":"p","s":["But too much disagreement can do the opposite. When we’re surrounded by very different views, the competing signals can make politics confusing and overwhelming. This can also feel socially uncomfortable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier research has found that people in ",["highly conflict-ridden social networks","https://doi.org/10.1017/S0003055402004264"]," sometimes pull back from politics to avoid straining relationships with friends, family and co-workers."]},{"k":"h","s":["What this means for Canada"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our data come from 2015, when Liberal Justin Trudeau ended up winning a majority government, but the campaign was ",["a tight three-way race for much of its run","https://www.utoronto.ca/news/election-2015-polling-despite-marked-increase-support-ndp-its-still-three-way-race-expert-says"],". There was a wide range of views across ridings, making it a suitable election for studying how disagreement relates to voting."]},{"k":"p","s":["We think the same forces are likely at work in later elections, including 2025. So how voters experience disagreement in their own communities may matter for turnout, not just how close the race is."]},{"k":"p","s":["The findings also matter when riding maps change. When boundaries are redrawn, like they were in Québec in ",["39 provincial ridings","https://www.electionsquebec.qc.ca/en/electoral-maps/review-of-quebecs-electoral-map/electoral-map-final-boundaries/"]," ahead of its recent election, the mix of neighbours who voters live among shifts too."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our study also adds to the debate about political division. Research on Canadian voting habits has focused on ",["how warmly or coldly people feel toward the other side","https://theconversation.com/canada-isnt-deeply-polarized-yet-what-new-research-reveals-about-partisan-animosity-267719"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Canada isn’t deeply polarized — yet. What new research reveals about partisan animosity","https://theconversation.com/canada-isnt-deeply-polarized-yet-what-new-research-reveals-about-partisan-animosity-267719"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Our results raise a different concern. People whose views closely mirror those around them are somewhat less likely to vote than those whose views differ moderately."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our study has a clear scope. It covers one election in a system where the candidate with the most votes wins each riding. Our survey results rely on stated intentions to vote, and show an association between how much people’s views differ from those around them and voter turnout. The next test is whether these findings held in 2025."]},{"k":"p","s":["The lesson, however, is worth taking seriously. A healthy democracy may depend not on eliminating political disagreement, but on keeping it within a range people can engage with."]}],"chars":5359},"https://theconversation.com/slapps-ndas-and-gendered-lawfare-how-the-rich-and-powerful-silence-victims-of-sexual-offences-296520":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"6fbcd0d7aa52703bfd967d2af2f2169246e6707987b68ed4a3c91f3c195fcd1e","read":"https://theconversation.com/slapps-ndas-and-gendered-lawfare-how-the-rich-and-powerful-silence-victims-of-sexual-offences-296520","bytes":182065,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Slapps, NDAs and gendered ‘lawfare’: how the rich and powerful silence victims of sexual offences","by":[{"n":"Francesca Farrington","r":"Lecturer in Law, School of Law and Social Justice, University of Liverpool"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T18:36:27Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The conviction of Russell Brand came nearly two decades after “Me Too” was coined. Yet the years the former comedian avoided accountability serve as a stark reminder of the dangers victims still face when speaking out. The truth is that women who name predators are increasingly at risk of legal proceedings."]},{"k":"p","s":["While the ",["#MeToo","https://theconversation.com/topics/metoo-45316"]," movement emboldened victims to speak truth to power, it also exposed the tactics offenders use to silence them. UN special rapporteur ",["Irene Khan","https://docs.un.org/en/A/76/258"],", described this as a “perverse twist” in the age of #MeToo."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Research","https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=6958538"]," has shed light on what’s really happening here – mechanisms designed to provide justice can be used to suppress victims and provide impunity for those with money and power. So how can this happen in countries that are supposed to be committed to fundamental rights and the rule of law?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Across the world, powerful people are evading scrutiny by threatening legal action that could leave their accusers ruined financially. When powerful people use the law, or even just the threat of it, to suppress criticism, it is known as strategic lawsuits against public participation (Slapp)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You might wonder why courts don’t simply dismiss these cases. In practice, it is rare that they even ",["make it before a judge","https://antislapp.uk/2025/10/16/nina-cresswell-response-report/"],", because the threat is often enough to push a settlement. For many, as ",["one victim said","https://antislapp.uk/2025/10/16/nina-cresswell-response-report/"],", “silence is the only way to survive”. The aim is not to win the case, but to turn the process of defending the action into a punishment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Gendered lawfare"]},{"k":"p","s":["Slapps take many forms. ",["Many people","https://youth.europa.eu/young-journalists/articles/daphnes-law-honouring-legacy-of-fearless-journalist-fight-press-freedom_en"]," might picture a corporation or politician suing a public watchdog. Less well known are Slapps targeting victims of sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV). Often referred to as a kind of gendered censorship or gendered lawfare, these lawsuits ",["are prevalent","https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=6958538"]," and equally chilling. Rather than seeking justice, these legal tactics are used to create fear, financial pressure and a culture of self-censorship."]},{"k":"p","s":["When reporting on SGBV, the ",["stakes are high enough","https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/sep/24/russell-brand-and-why-the-allegations-took-so-long-to-surface"]," for large media organisations. So imagine how high they are for victims. In 2023, a woman called ",["Nina Cresswell","https://antislapp.uk/project/nina-cresswell/"]," shared her story of sexual abuse on social media. It related to an incident in 2010, and Cresswell said she was motivated to speak out by guilt at the thought of another woman suffering what she had gone through."]},{"k":"p","s":["But just days later, her alleged abuser sued her for defamation. The lawsuit did three things. By suing Cresswell, the perpetrator denied the abuse, attacked his accuser, and recast himself as the victim. This tactic is known as Darvo – Deny, Attack, Reverse Victim and Offender. It has become an ",["integral part","https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=6958538"]," of gendered-Slapp suits. Cresswell won her case, but she lost almost ",["three years of her life","https://antislapp.uk/2025/10/16/nina-cresswell-response-report/"]," to litigation. No police action was taken against the man."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Brand has been accused","https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/story/2023-09-16/russell-brand-rape-sexual-assault-allegations-denial-video-times-channel-4?googsrc=ai-uk"]," of similar tactics. He reportedly obtained ",["an anti-harassment injunction","https://taxpolicy.org.uk/2026/11/07/russell-brand-secret-injunction/"]," against ",["Szilvia Berki","https://www.thetimes.com/uk/law/article/russell-brand-gagging-order-accuser-sx799n956"]," after she made allegations against him. The injunction – which is still in place – is far-reaching and prohibits Berki from repeating her allegations, including to friends and family."]},{"k":"p","s":["She was left with £50,000 in legal costs, and the judge authorised Brand’s lawyers to begin ",["bankruptcy proceedings","https://www.thetimes.com/uk/law/article/russell-brand-gagging-order-accuser-sx799n956"]," against her. While the full story behind the injunction appears to be complicated, Berki’s experience shows the scope of these gagging orders and the financial cost associated with fighting one."]},{"k":"p","s":["Entertainer ",["David Walliams","https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/nov/10/david-walliams-allegations-high-court-case-key-legal-issues?googsrc=ai-uk"]," attempted to secure an injunction to suppress claims of sexual misconduct. While he denies all allegations against him, his application was refused and the findings of investigations by ",["The Guardian","https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/ng-interactive/2026/nov/10/david-walliams-accused-sex-grooming-allegations-young-women"]," and ",["ITV News","https://www.itv.com/news/2026-11-10/david-walliams-accused-of-preying-on-teenage-girls-as-young-as-15?googsrc=ai-uk"]," are now public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Non-disclosure agreements (NDAs) are also a major part of gendered censorship. For years, contracts were used to silence victims and witnesses of SGBV. ",["Zelda Perkins","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/08/theres-nowhere-for-them-to-hide-any-more-zelda-perkins-on-harvey-weinstein-and-ndas"],", a former personal assistant to disgraced US film producer Harvey Weinstein, was bound by an NDA after she tried to expose his predatory behaviour."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a remarkable act of courage, she broke her NDA, exposing herself to substantial legal risk. She has been campaigning for reform ever since. On an episode of the ",["News Agents podcast","https://www.globalplayer.com/podcasts/episodes/7Ds3AeM/"],", Perkins revealed that she believes there are several women who entered into NDAs with Brand."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ending gendered censorship"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no silver bullet in this struggle, yet there has been some progress. In the UK, the ",["Victims and Courts Act 2026","https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2026/19/section/6"]," voids any provision in an agreement that prevents a disclosure relating to criminal conduct. And the ",["Employment Rights Act 2025","https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2025/36/section/24"]," protects a worker’s right to disclose harassment and discrimination."]},{"k":"p","s":["But more must be done. ",["Perkins warned","https://www.globalplayer.com/podcasts/episodes/7Ds3AeM/"]," that Slapps – “the evil cousin of NDAs”, remain a real threat to victims. When it comes to combatting them, the UK lags behind other countries. In the UK, Slapp targets are only protected when reporting on ",["economic and financial crime","https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2023/56/part/5/crossheading/power-to-strike-out-certain-claims/enacted"],", and even then, only to a ",["limited extent","https://www.birmingham.ac.uk/news/2025/new-mechanism-needed-in-english-law-to-slap-down-slapps-study"],". Victims of SGBV are left largely unprotected."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Parliament is debating","https://antislapp.uk/2026/06/16/two-private-members-bills-in-both-houses-place-anti-slapp-reform-firmly-on-the-parliamentary-agenda/"]," whether to extend protections to everyone speaking out on public interest matters. But recent reports have been a reminder that stronger anti-Slapp protections are needed to prevent the law becoming an instrument of the powerful against those alleging abuse."]}],"chars":5197},"https://theconversation.com/dari-tni-run-hingga-primarox-waspada-normalisasi-militerisme-di-panggung-olahraga-sipil-292782":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"0933fae4c323f086de0b38c43cf47f766bbae7b406e5c09118ce5b07e4fc8b3c","read":"https://theconversation.com/dari-tni-run-hingga-primarox-waspada-normalisasi-militerisme-di-panggung-olahraga-sipil-292782","bytes":181254,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Dari TNI Run hingga PRIMAROX: Waspada normalisasi militerisme di panggung olahraga sipil","by":[{"n":"Dini Dwi Kusumaningrum","r":"Peneliti, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"}],"pub":"2026-10-13T06:50:41Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Simbol militer dalam olahraga populer berpotensi menormalkan kehadiran militer di ruang sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Kesetaraan di arena olahraga tidak menghapus ketimpangan kuasa antara militer dan warga sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Keakraban dengan militer tidak boleh menggeser tuntutan akuntabilitas dan supremasi sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lari, angkat beban, membalik ban raksasa, lalu mengunggah pencapaiannya ke media sosial sudah jadi bagian dari gaya hidup performatif masyarakat saat ini."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, bagaimana jika tantangan kebugaran itu menggunakan perlengkapan militer, lengkap dengan kehadiran tank dan kendaraan taktis di arena lomba?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fenomena ini kian umum terlihat di berbagai event seperti ",["PRIMAROX Panglima TNI Cup 2026 di Indonesia Convention Exhibition (ICE) BSD, Kabupaten Tangerang","https://ice-indonesia.com/id/event/event_list/primarox-2026"],". Ada juga ",["TNI Run 2026 di Monas","https://megapolitan.antaranews.com/berita/550820/tni-run-2026-diikuti-ribuan-peserta-serta-sukses-catatkan-rekor-muri"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Berbagai event tersebut layaknya perhelatan ",["HYROX","https://www.instagram.com/p/Dck2f4LEgnm/"]," dan lari pada umumnya. Bedanya, ada sejumlah tantangan menggunakan ",["perlengkapan bernuansa militer","https://www.sandboxx.us/news/family-resources/health-and-wellness/keep-fit-on-deployment-with-these-improvised-workout-equipment-ideas/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sebelum memasuki arena, pengunjung disambut pameran tank, kendaraan taktis TNI, dan café van yang menampilkan lirik Hymne Komando Kopassus TNI AD: “Lebih baik pulang nama daripada gagal dalam tugas”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terpampang juga Ammo box carry yang mengharuskan peserta membawa kotak yang terinspirasi dari perlengkapan logistik militer. Sementara itu, tire flip menggunakan ban kendaraan taktis Anoa milik TNI dengan berat sekitar 84 kilogram. Corak militer juga hadir dalam desain jersey acara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, di balik keseruan kompetisi, kita bisa bertanya: apa yang bisa terjadi ketika simbol militer semakin akrab dalam kehidupan sipil? Padahal, perluasan peran militer dalam demokrasi masih menjadi perdebatan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Selamat datang era ‘fitness-entertainment’: Bagaimana peluang cuan hyrox setelah tren padel?","https://theconversation.com/selamat-datang-era-fitness-entertainment-bagaimana-peluang-cuan-hyrox-setelah-tren-padel-277854"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Ketika simbol militer menjadi bagian dari gaya hidup"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi penggemar kebugaran, perlengkapan militer yang dipamerkan mungkin sekadar tantangan untuk menguji kekuatan, daya tahan, dan memberikan pengalaman unik baru. Namun, ada hal yang penting diamati dalam konteks ini."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Sosiolog Erving Goffman","https://ejurnal.ubk.ac.id/oratio/en/article/view/63?utm"]," menjelaskan bahwa interaksi sosial sebagai semacam pertunjukan. Dalam kehidupan sehari-hari, orang menampilkan identitas melalui penampilan, perilaku, bahasa, dan lingkungan. Semua itu membentuk kesan yang ditangkap orang lain."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kerangka ini membantu kita memahami bagaimana identitas militer ditampilkan dalam acara olahraga. Di arena yang dipenuhi pelari, penggemar fitness, keluarga, dan komunitas, prajurit tidak hanya tampil sebagai anggota institusi pertahanan, tetapi juga sebagai sesama peserta olahraga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalahnya, citra yang ditampilkan tidak pernah sepenuhnya netral. Ketika militer hadir melalui aktivitas yang menyenangkan, perhatian publik dapat lebih tertuju pada kebugaran, solidaritas, dan semangat kompetisi daripada pada kewenangan institusi tersebut atau batas perannya dalam negara demokratis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di pihak lain, masyarakat sipil tidak sekadar menyaksikan simbol militer dari kejauhan, melainkan berinteraksi dengannya melalui pengalaman fisik."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian tentang olahraga dan militerisme Inggris","https://www.tandfonline.com/servlet/linkout?type=Scholix&url=https%3A%2F%2Fdx.doi.org%2F10.1177%252F0038038512453795"]," menunjukkan bagaimana budaya populer dan olahraga dapat membantu membangun citra kepahlawanan militer sekaligus menormalkan nilai-nilai militerisme."]},{"k":"p","s":["Temuan itu tidak otomatis membuktikan bahwa PRIMAROX memiliki agenda serupa, tetapi setidaknya memberi kerangka untuk mempertanyakan bagaimana simbol militer memperoleh penerimaan melalui ruang yang terasa jauh dari politik."]},{"k":"h","s":["Membaca arah relasi kuasa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Di arena olahraga, prajurit dan warga sipil tampak setara: sama-sama berlari, mengangkat beban, dan menghadapi tantangan fisik. Namun, kesetaraan sebagai peserta kompetisi tidak berarti kesetaraan dalam relasi kuasa."]},{"k":"p","s":["TNI memiliki kewenangan negara, struktur komando, dan fungsi pertahanan yang tidak dimiliki warga sipil. Karena itu, kehadiran militer di ruang publik tidak cukup dibaca sebagai pertemuan dua kelompok yang berbagi hobi. Kita juga perlu bertanya siapa yang memiliki kuasa menentukan batas keterlibatan militer dalam kehidupan sipil, serta bagaimana kewenangan itu diawasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pertanyaan tersebut relevan dalam konteks sejarah Indonesia. Pada masa Orde Baru, ",["doktrin Dwifungsi ABRI","https://ejournal.fisip.unjani.ac.id/index.php/jurnal-academia-praja/article/view/182"]," memberikan militer peran dalam pertahanan sekaligus kehidupan sosial-politik. Reformasi 1998 kemudian ",["mendorong perubahan hubungan sipil–militer","https://journal.unnes.ac.id/sju/jih/article/view/36973"],", termasuk pemisahan TNI dan Polri serta upaya memperkuat supremasi sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kini, perdebatan kembali mengemuka setelah pengesahan ",["Undang-Undang Nomor 3 Tahun 2025","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/319166/uu-no-3-tahun-2025?utm"]," yang merevisi UU TNI."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perubahan ketentuan penempatan prajurit aktif di kementerian dan lembaga negara memunculkan kekhawatiran akademisi mengenai batas kewenangan militer dan pengawasan sipil. ",["Kajian Victor Imanuel W. Nalle pada 2026","https://repositori.ukdc.ac.id/id/eprint/2595/"]," juga menempatkan revisi tersebut dalam dinamika politik dan perubahan relasi sipil–militer pasca-Reformasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam konteks ini, persoalannya bukan membuktikan bahwa satu ajang olahraga menyebabkan militerisme, melainkan bagaimana keakraban simbolik dengan militer berkembang bersamaan dengan perdebatan mengenai perluasan peran institusinya."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dari keakraban menuju pertanyaan demokrasi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Olahraga bukan ruang yang terpisah dari politik–justru dapat menjadi tempat institusi membangun citra, memperoleh perhatian, dan membentuk hubungan dengan masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika ",["simbol militer dikemas","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/0038038512453795"]," sebagai tantangan yang seru dan layak dibagikan di media sosial, citra institusi dapat ",["lebih mudah diterima","https://academic.oup.com/isr/article/23/3/1046/5866651"]," tanpa disertai pembicaraan mengenai akuntabilitas dan batas kewenangannya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi generasi muda yang akrab dengan komunitas lari dan kebugaran, pertanyaan ini bukan ajakan untuk mencurigai setiap acara yang melibatkan TNI. Sebaliknya, ini merupakan ajakan untuk tidak berhenti pada pengalaman baru yang menyenangkan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kita perlu membedakan penghargaan terhadap kemampuan individu prajurit dari penerimaan tanpa kritik terhadap institusi militer. Disiplin dan ketahanan fisik tidak dengan sendirinya membuktikan bahwa perluasan peran militer dalam urusan sipil dapat dibenarkan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam demokrasi, kedekatan militer dengan masyarakat tidak boleh menggantikan kebutuhan akan pengawasan sipil. Sebab, yang perlu dijaga bukan sekadar batas antara arena olahraga dan arena politik, melainkan batas kewenangan antara institusi bersenjata dan masyarakat sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keakraban militer dengan warga sipil seharusnya membuat kita semakin memahami peran militer dalam demokrasi–jangan sampai justru membuat kita semakin jarang mempertanyakannya."]}],"chars":6349},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"e5e4d098bc1cc9cadebfcc39585af322c2225087afe3ade228e5e5dbb2e68f0f","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","bytes":98206,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Kenya travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-19T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-06T17:00:48+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kenya-Somalia border and northern parts of the east coast"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the risk of terrorism from groups based in Somalia, FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mandera County"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tarbaj and Wajir East constituencies in Wajir County, except for Wajir Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas of Wajir County within 60km of Kenya’s border with Somalia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Garissa County - except for Garissa Town, the constituency of Lagdera and the areas of Balambala constituency which lie north and west of the main road which runs from Saka on the Tana River up to the intersection with the C81 Road"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lamu County, except for Lamu Island and Manda Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Garissa Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tana River County north of the Tana River as far as the town of Saka"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River"]},{"k":"li","s":["Moyale Town and up to 5km around it, including to the border with Ethiopia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Kenya set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Kenyan High Commission in the UK","https://www.kenyahighcom.org.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Kenya, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["apply online for electronic travel authorisation","https://www.etakenya.go.ke/en"]," in advance of travel. The local authorities recommend applying at least 2 weeks before your departure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers who currently hold a visa can continue to travel using their visa until it expires."]},{"k":"p","s":["For information on work permits and residency, check the ",["Kenyan Department of Immigration","https://immigration.go.ke/"]," requirements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mandatory travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 5 October 2026, most travellers visiting Kenya for less than 12 months must have Kenyan Government-provided travel health insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you require an Electronic Travel Authorisation (eTA), you must buy this insurance as part of the application process. If you already hold a valid eTA, you must obtain the insurance through the ",["Kenyan eCitizen insurance portal","https://insurance.ecitizen.go.ke/dashboard"],". Foreign travel insurance policies are not accepted in place of this requirement."]},{"k":"p","s":["The insurance is valid for 90 days and can be used for multiple entries into Kenya during that period."]},{"k":"p","s":["The requirement does not apply to Kenyan citizens, holders of valid Kenyan residence status, citizens of East African Community partner states, or transit passengers that are not passing through Kenyan immigration control."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also make sure you have travel insurance that covers your individual needs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Kenya, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Kenya guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/117/kenya#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola screening"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Government of Kenya has confirmed cases of Ebola. Public health measures are in place, including contact tracing, surveillance, border screening and quarantine for people considered at risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers arriving in Kenya, particularly those coming from Uganda, Ethiopia and the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), may be subject to enhanced health screening measures due to the ongoing Ebola outbreak centred in the DRC. The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Kenyan authorities provide public health information through the Jali Health Chatbot. To access the service, save +(254) 700 719 719 to your phone and send “Hello” by Whatsapp to access automated health information and guidance. This is not a staffed helpline."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Kenya","https://www.kenyagovisas.com/news/kenya-customs-regulations"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking drones into Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import or export drones without prior approval from the ",["Kenya Civil Aviation Authority (KCAA)","https://www.kcaa.or.ke/"],". Contact the KCAA well in advance of travel if you wish to bring a drone to Kenya."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Kenya."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened threat of terrorism across Kenya. Attacks could target westerners, including British nationals. These could occur at any time including at religious events, public holidays or celebrations. Attacks are indiscriminate and could occur in places visited by foreigners, including tourists, such as, but not limited to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels, bars, restaurants and nightclubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting events"]},{"k":"li","s":["supermarkets and shopping centres"]},{"k":"li","s":["beaches"]},{"k":"li","s":["safari parks"]},{"k":"li","s":["commercial and government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["diplomatic premises"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be particularly alert in these places. If you go regularly to any location, try to vary timings and patterns of movement. Always travel during daylight hours if possible. Look at the security arrangements in buildings you visit, including bag searches, physical security and guards. The main terrorist threat is from extremists linked to Al Shabaab – an Al Qaida-affiliated militant group in Somalia. Al Shabaab has issued threats and carried out attacks against Kenya, in part, due to Kenyan military intervention in Somalia. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent significant attacks include :"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2020 Al Shabaab conducted an attack on a military airstrip in Lamu County, killing 3 people"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2019 there was an attack at the hotel and commercial complex at 14 Riverside in Nairobi, resulting in injuries and loss of life"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is some evidence of growing support for Daesh (formerly ISIL) in Kenya. On 4 January 2024 Daesh published a statement calling for a new global campaign of terrorism including a specific focus on western and Jewish targets. This statement and the ongoing conflict in Israel and Palestine could increase the likelihood of terrorist attacks that affect British nationals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lamu Island and Manda Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers to Lamu Island and Manda Island should be particularly vigilant given the close proximity of these islands to the Lamu County mainland. You should only travel to the islands by air to Lamu airport (a civilian airport on Manda Island), and not by road. The only commercial option for air travel to or from Lamu Island and Manda Island is through Lamu airport. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist kidnap across Kenya. You should be alert to the heightened threat of terrorist kidnapping targeting westerners, including British nationals. Westerners have been the target of kidnaps in northern counties bordering Somalia and coastal counties. Further kidnaps are very likely."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests, demonstrations and strikes are common in Kenya, particularly in Nairobi. These events often cause traffic disruption and can lead to violence. A number of demonstrators have been injured and killed in recent years. The situation could change quickly, especially on key dates, such as anniversaries of previous protests. Stay away from political gatherings and large crowds and monitor local media to see when and where major protests are likely. Follow local news and the instructions of local authorities closely."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent incidents of violent crime including mugging, armed robbery and carjacking, particularly in the large cities and on major highways."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although uncommon, violent crimes have resulted in the deaths of British nationals, including during daylight hours."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid walking alone in isolated areas, including in daylight. Criminals might target you directly, so be aware of your surroundings and make sure people know where you are and when you are due to return. The risks are higher in some areas of major cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Nairobi:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Eastleigh"]},{"k":"li","s":["Central Business District"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mathare, Kibera and slum areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Mombasa:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the Old Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["on and around the Likoni Ferry, which links Mombasa to the southern resorts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime rates are often higher around the Christmas and New Year period so take extra precautions at this time of year."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bag-snatching is common in bus stations, railway stations and airports. Be vigilant and take note of any security advice given by your hotel, employer or your hosts. If you’re attacked, do not resist. Avoid carrying large sums of money or wearing expensive-looking jewellery or watches."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always drive with windows closed and doors locked. When driving outside of cities and in remote areas, consider driving in convoy. Avoid driving at night if possible. Carjackers may set up bogus checkpoints. See ",["Transport risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#transport-risks"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beware of thieves posing as police officers or private security guards. It’s a technique used by criminals to take charge of valuables, passports and vehicles and steal them. Always ask for identification."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink and food spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not accept drinks or food from strangers in bars or clubs. Criminals spike drinks to weaken and confuse their victims and then commit theft or sexual assault."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Attacks and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sexual assaults are rare, but do happen, and can affect both male and female travellers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Social media and dating apps"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals can use dating apps to identify victims to rob or sexually assault. There has been an increase in criminals targeting LGBT+ travellers in particular. Be cautious when using social media and dating apps. If you decide to meet someone, meet in a well-lit, public place and make sure that someone knows where you are."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry ID. A copy of your passport is normally acceptable, but police officers may insist on seeing the original document so keep it within a reasonable travelling distance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["The coastal areas of Kenya are mainly Muslim. Show courtesy by dressing conservatively away from tourist resorts and hotels – particularly in Mombasa. Wearing holiday-style clothing is likely to get negative attention at religious sites or buildings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to smoke in any public place in Kenya, except in designated smoking areas. If you smoke in a prohibited place, you could get a fine of up to 50,000 Kenyan shillings or up to 6 months in prison."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re convicted of using illegal drugs in Kenya, you will get a heavy fine and prison sentence. The penalty for possession is up to 10 years in prison. People found to be trafficking illegal drugs could face life imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photographs of official buildings, including embassies, or at airports. You could be arrested if caught."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal and same-sex relationships are not tolerated in Kenya’s conservative society. Showing affection in public could lead to arrest and imprisonment. See the ‘Social media and dating apps’ subheading for more advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade any of its parts without a licence. If you are caught buying or trafficking banned goods, you could face a fine or prison sentence."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Game reserves and national parks"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting game reserves, use reputable tour operators and arrive at your destination in daylight hours. Do not buy safari tours from touts. Always follow park regulations and advice from wardens."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are risks associated with viewing wildlife, particularly on foot or at close range. Swimming in rivers and lakes is illegal in national parks and is best avoided elsewhere due the dangers from wildlife and waterborne diseases."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must hire a local guide on certain hikes in Kenya. Be conscious of the risk from wildlife and do not approach wild animals. Make sure your travel insurance covers all your planned activities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk when hiking in high-altitude areas, including on Mount Kenya. Read about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Kenya, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence in Kenya for up to 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["After 3 months, you’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying longer or living in Kenya, you’ll need to get a Kenyan driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are often poor. There is a risk of vehicle crime – see ",["Crime","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#crime"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Jomo Kenyatta International Airport to Nairobi City"]},{"k":"p","s":["For travel between Jomo Kenyatta International Airport and Nairobi City, use the Mombasa Road or the Nairobi Expressway. There is a higher risk of carjacking on the old airport road (Airport South Road) and Jogoo Road."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Mombasa Road can get very busy during rush hour, and check-in can take several hours. Allow plenty of time to get to the airport. A vehicle security check outside the airport may add to your journey time."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel in remote areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local media and take care in all remote areas. ",["The Kenya Tourism Federation Safety and Communication Center","https://ktf.co.ke/?page_id=857"]," provides tourist advice and emergency help."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bus travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been serious accidents involving long-distance buses and minibuses (‘matatus’). The accidents are often due to poor maintenance and speeding. Often minibuses are uninsured. Check operators’ safety standards."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent minibus hijackings and robberies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving fines"]},{"k":"p","s":["On-the-spot fines from traffic police are common but illegal. If a traffic police officer stops you, ask them to issue you with the correct paperwork."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you charter a private aircraft, check with the company about the condition of the aircraft and runways. If the air crew does not include a safety pilot, qualified to take over the controls, find another company that does."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Passenger trains run between Nairobi and Mombasa. Take care of your belongings while on the train and at railway stations. If you leave your compartment, take your valuables with you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Piracy and armed robbery off the coast of Somalia, in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean remain a significant threat."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["piracy and armed robbery at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kenya lies on an active fault and tremors occur from time to time. The last significant earthquake to affect the region was of magnitude 5.2 in 2007."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Kenya. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kenya-Somalia border and northern parts of the east coast"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the risk of terrorism from groups based in Somalia, FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mandera County"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tarbaj and Wajir East constituencies in Wajir County, except for Wajir Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas of Wajir County within 60km of Kenya’s border with Somalia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Garissa County - except for Garissa Town, the constituency of Lagdera and the areas of Balambala constituency which lie north and west of the main road which runs from Saka on the Tana River up to the intersection with the C81 Road"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lamu County, except for Lamu Island and Manda Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Garissa Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tana River County north of the Tana River as far as the town of Saka"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River"]},{"k":"li","s":["Moyale Town and up to 5km around it, including to the border with Ethiopia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been frequent attacks in the north-eastern border regions, most of which were attributed to Al Shabaab."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks have killed members of the Kenyan security forces as well as civilians. The Kenyan security forces have increased their presence in the affected areas. Armed militia groups operate within the Boni National Reserve and along the border with Somalia. See ",["Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lamu Island and Manda Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to Lamu Island or Manda Island, you should fly to Lamu Airport (a civilian airport on Manda Island). Do not travel by road. See ",["Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Jomo Kenyatta International Airport to Nairobi City"]},{"k":"p","s":["For travel between Jomo Kenyatta International Airport and Nairobi City, you should use the Mombasa Road or the Nairobi Expressway. See ",["Transport risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#transport-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["North and north-east Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rural areas, particularly in the north and north-east of Kenya, occasionally experience cattle rustling, banditry and ethnic clashes. Foreign nationals are not usually the target, but you should take great care."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Turkana, West Pokot, Elgeyo-Marakwet, Baringo,Samburu, Laikipia, Meru and Isiolo counties"]},{"k":"p","s":["Security operations continue in parts of these counties due to banditry ,cattle rustling and intercommunal violence. While previous dusk-to-dawn curfews have largely been lifted, movement restrictions may still be introduced during security operations, particularly in hotspots such as the Turkana–West Pokot border, Kerio Valley (Elgeyo-Marakwet) and remote areas of Samburu, and Baringo. Follow local security measures and use caution."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kenya-Ethiopia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since October 2026, violence in the Ethiopian town of Moyale has affected the border area, including on the Kenyan side. There have been reports of stray gunfire, unexploded ordnance and projectiles landing in and up to 3km around the Kenyan town of Moyale, resulting in fatalities and injuries. There have also been reports of disruption at the Moyale border crossing. The security situation remains unpredictable and could deteriorate without warning."]},{"k":"p","s":["If crossing the Kenya-Ethiopia border at Moyale, stay alert to developments and follow the instructions of local authorities. Vehicles crossing the Kenya-Ethiopia border at Moyale should stay on the A2 road and travel directly to Marsabit before breaking your journey."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["FCDO Travel Advice for Ethiopia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ethiopia"]," before crossing the border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mount Elgon"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a significant security presence in Mount Elgon because of armed clashes. Further incidents are possible. Seek local advice before you set off."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Kenya","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/117/kenya#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Kenya","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/117/kenya"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"li","s":["ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Kenya. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 6 October 2026, the Kenyan Ministry of Health confirmed its first imported case of Ebola. The government is continuing to implement public health measures in response, including contact tracing, surveillance, and border screening, as well as quarantine arrangements for individuals deemed at risk. Follow the advice of local authorities and monitor updates from the ",["Kenyan Ministry of Health","https://www.health.go.ke/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro has information on ",["Ebola Disease","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/news/ebola-disease-in-drc-and-uganda"]," and ",["general information on Ebola and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheets/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],". Some countries may have additional health screening requirements for travellers arriving from Kenya. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," for countries you are travelling to or transiting through."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Health Security Agency has ",["Ebola information for humanitarian or healthcare workers","https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/ebola-virus-disease-clinical-management-and-guidance"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kenya-list-of-medical-facilities/kenya-doctors"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-kenya"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Kenya Tourism Federation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kenya Tourism Federation’s ",["Safety and Communication Center","https://ktf.co.ke/?page_id=857"]," provides tourist advice and emergency help."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Kenya"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Kenya"]," in Kenya"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kenya-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kenya-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’ve been a ",["victim of rape or sexual assault in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kenya-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault/kenya-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/kenya/british-high-commission-nairobi"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Keny","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-kenya"]," a on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":25625,"change":"FCDO now advises against all but essential travel to Moyale Town and up to 5km around it, including to the border with Ethiopia. Updated information about the Kenya-Ethiopia border ('Warnings and insurance' and 'Regional risks' pages)."}};
